---
title: "The City That Planted a Thousand Rooftops"
summary: "A fictional coastal town reimagines its skyline with gardens, pollinator paths, and neighborhood volunteers."
category: Environment
date: 2026-11-10
author: "Maya Ellis"
---

In the imaginary coastal city of Bellhaven, residents are looking up for a new kind of public space. Over the past two years, local volunteers have transformed one thousand flat rooftops into small gardens.

## A different kind of skyline

The project began with a simple question: what if unused rooftops could help cool the city and bring neighbors together? A fictional community group called Skyward Gardens organized planting days and shared tools.

Some roofs now grow herbs. Others host native flowers, shallow rainwater beds, or benches where residents can watch the sunset.

## Small spaces, shared effort

Organizers say the project is less about a single dramatic solution and more about the value of many small changes. Each participating building chooses its own plants and maintenance schedule.

Bellhaven, its organizations, and this initiative are entirely fictional. This story is a sample of the kind of local reporting this website could publish.
